  <div class="code-explanation">
    <h3>What's happening here</h3>
    <p>The existing Markdown-first demo now starts with a manually triggered,
      staged proposal. It is not an autonomous issue publisher.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Trigger</strong> — a deliberate <code>workflow_dispatch</code>, not a new schedule.</li>
      <li><strong>Inference</strong> — <code>copilot-requests: write</code> uses the Actions token
        where organization policy and billing allow it; personal repositories may need
        the documented PAT alternative.</li>
      <li><strong>Repository access</strong> — scoped read permissions and GitHub toolsets.</li>
      <li><strong>Bounded output</strong> — at most one issue proposal, with evidence and uncertainty.</li>
      <li><strong>Staged output</strong> — previews the proposed write; it is not an approval queue.</li>
      <li><strong>Human handoff</strong> — inspect the proposal, then explicitly decide what work to accept.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Copy this source into a disposable repository's <code>.github/workflows/</code>,
      compile it with <code>gh aw compile</code>, and review both the source and generated
      <code>.lock.yml</code> before committing. Frontmatter changes require recompilation;
      the Markdown body is loaded at runtime.</p>
    <p><strong>Validation:</strong> compiler-checked with gh-aw v1.2.2;
      model inference and cloud execution were not run for this refresh.</p>
    <p><a href="https://github.github.com/gh-aw/reference/auth/">Authentication reference</a>
